A '''gang''' of [[Nikto]] [[Mercenary|mercenaries]] was active on [[Arvala-7]] in [[9 ABY]], and had in their captivity [[Din Grogu|a child]] that was the [[Yoda's species|same species]] as former [[Jedi]] [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]].

==History==
During the [[New Republic Era]], a [[mercenary]] [[company]] composed of [[Nikto]] was active on Arvala-7<ref name="Chapter 1" /> in [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Fragment Date" /> and was headquartered in an [[Nikto hideout|encampment]] that could only be accessed by riding a [[blurrg]]. Their presence on the [[planet]] created an endless stream of criminals and violence. At one point, they had in their possession an infant later referred to as "[[Din Grogu|the asset]]," which was of the same [[Yoda's species|species]] as the former [[Jedi]] [[Grand Master]] [[Yoda]]. Eventually, word spread that the mercenary group had the individual, and many sought to capture it. The violence created by the mercenaries brought the [[Ugnaught]] [[moisture farmer]] [[Kuiil]] to aid those who sought to capture "the asset," but they all failed and [[Death|died]].<ref name="Chapter 1" />

Eventually, a [[bounty hunter]] known as "[[Din Djarin|the Mandalorian]]" was hired by a [[The Client|member]] of an [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|Imperial remnant]]. When at the encampment, the [[Mandalorian]] encountered [[IG-11]], who was also hired to deal with "the asset," albeit with instructions to kill it. Both [[bounty]] hunters worked together to destroy the mercenary group, after which the Mandalorian was forced to kill IG-11 to prevent the [[droid]] from killing "the asset."<ref name="Chapter 1" />

